{
  "A command buffer draw of a shader with no SubShader in reach draws its first SubShader in the Editor; Unbound's renderer keeps its earlier choice (the error shader for another pipeline's SubShaders, nothing past the LOD limit, measured for camera renders in tests/projects/shaderpasscount). The queries answer from the first SubShader as measured.": [
    "select.empty.SelF.drawn",
    "select.lower.SelF.drawn",
    "select.lod10.drawn"
  ],
  "The Editor's keyword space has URP's foveated rendering keyword, declared in a branch for Metal and PS5 only (FoveatedRenderingKeywords.hlsl); Unbound reads the branches active on the running device. Hypothesis, unmeasured: the Editor unites the declarations of every shader platform its installed build targets compile for (iOS here), while a branch for an uninstalled one (Direct3D 11, tests/projects/shaderkeywords D3D_ONLY) declares nothing.": [
    "keywords.Universal Render Pipeline/Unlit.count",
    "keywords.Universal Render Pipeline/Unlit.names",
    "keywords.Universal Render Pipeline/Unlit.flags",
    "keywords.Universal Render Pipeline/Particles/Lit.count",
    "keywords.Universal Render Pipeline/Particles/Lit.names",
    "keywords.Universal Render Pipeline/Particles/Lit.flags",
    "keywords.Hidden/Universal Render Pipeline/StencilDeferred.count",
    "keywords.Hidden/Universal Render Pipeline/StencilDeferred.names",
    "keywords.Hidden/Universal Render Pipeline/StencilDeferred.flags"
  ],
  "The Editor loads every project shader as the project opens, so a new pipeline tag reports each loaded shader's undefined Queue again ('Shader Unknown'); Unbound reads a shader when it is first asked for, and the probe asks for its Queue shaders after the pipeline tag last changed.": [
    "queue.errors.unknown"
  ],
  "MeshUtility.Optimize reorders the triangles for the vertex cache and the vertices by first use with Unity's own optimizer, which is not reproduced: Unbound leaves the mesh as it is (the member stays a stub).": [
    "meshUtility.optimized.vertices",
    "meshUtility.optimized.uv",
    "meshUtility.optimized.triangles",
    "meshUtility.grid.vertices",
    "meshUtility.grid.triangles"
  ],
  "A PerRendererData texture property without a texture reads back the Editor's 'textureExternal' texture through MaterialProperty.textureValue (the material itself answers null); where it comes from is not measured.": [
    "materialProperty._Per.texture"
  ],
  "The physical camera's projection differs from the Editor's in the last bits of m00 and m11 (Unbound computes 2 * focalLength / sensor width; the Editor's arithmetic is not reproduced). Anamorphism changes neither (both captures show the same matrix with it set and at 0).": [
    "anamorphism.projection",
    "anamorphism.projection0"
  ],
  "The renderer runs no geometry or tessellation stage: for a shader whose first SubShader has such a pass it draws the next SubShader (warned once per shader), while the Editor's OpenGL Core and Vulkan devices draw the first, which the queries answer from too. What is drawn and the pass lists Material.FindPass under a render pipeline, GetPassName, SetPass and FindPassTagValue read are the drawn SubShader's, while passCount answers from the first.": [
    "select.restricted.SelG.drawn",
    "select.restricted.SelT.drawn",
    "select.restricted.SelG.stagePass",
    "select.restricted.SelT.stagePass"
  ]
}
